  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef's Combinatorial Games Competition is starting again this year, and the qualification round is happening right now! This time, Chef is keeping it simple ― there will be two-player games with the following rules:\n\n\nInitially, the players are given an integer sequence SSS.\nThe players alternate turns.\nIn each turn, the current player must choose one or more elements of the current sequence SSS such that the values of all chosen elements are identical, and erase these elements from SSS.\nWhen a player cannot choose anything (the sequence SSS is already empty), this player loses the game.\nSince Chef is currently busy planning for the finals, he does not have time to prepare sequences for all qualification games. Instead, he chose a large sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and he wants to use its contiguous subsequences for the games. To get a idea of how these games will turn out, Chef wants you to answer QQQ queries. In each query, you are given a subsequence AL,AL+1,…,ARA_L, A_{L+1}, \\ldots, A_RAL​,AL+1​,…,AR​, and you have to find the number of winning moves the first player can play on the first turn. Since this number can be quite large, compute it modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.\n\nAssume that both players play optimally. The queries are independent ― the sequence AAA does not change.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\le T \\le 51≤T≤5",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\le N, Q \\le 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):**",
      "N,Q≤100N, Q \\le 100N,Q≤100",
      "Ai≤105A_i \\le 10^5Ai​≤105 for each valid iii",
      "**Subtask #2 (20 points):** N,Q≤103N, Q \\le 10^3N,Q≤103"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains a single integer QQQ.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers LLL and RRR describing a query.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of winning moves of the first player modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n5\n1 2 1 2 2\n3\n1 1\n2 3\n2 5",
        "output": "1\n0\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1:\n\nIn the first game, there is only one move and it is a winning move for the first player.\nIn the second game, the second player can always win regardless of the first player's move.\nIn the third game, the first player can choose the subset of elements with indices {2,4}\\{2, 4\\}{2,4}, {2,5}\\{2, 5\\}{2,5} or {4,5}\\{4, 5\\}{4,5} (in the input sequence AAA) to ensure his victory in the future."
      }
    ]
  },
